{
 "turns_text": [
  "[SEG0001] person_1 (NURSE): Morning. I already checked him in. Blood pressure is 152 over 88, pulse 102, temperature 37.1 celsius, oxygen sat 98 percent, and his respiratory rate is 18.",
  "[SEG0002] person_2 (DOCTOR): Thank you. Please sit, sir. I'm Dr. Shah. What brings you in this morning?",
  "[SEG0003] person_3 (PATIENT): Good morning, doctor. I have a sudden, quite severe pain in the right loin, and it runs down into the groin. That is why I came.",
  "[SEG0004] person_2 (DOCTOR): I'm sorry. About what time did it start?",
  "[SEG0005] person_3 (PATIENT): It began very suddenly, around two this morning, so that is, umm, six or seven hours. I would put it at a seven, perhaps an eight when it surges, and moving about makes it worse.",
  "[SEG0006] person_4 (CAREGIVER): I'm Helen, his caregiver. I stay with him on weekdays. He was up pacing, and he threw up once, a little after three.",
  "[SEG0007] person_3 (PATIENT): Yes, that is right. I vomited the one time, and I have not vomited since. There was blood in the urine when I urinated, around four.",
  "[SEG0008] person_2 (DOCTOR): Visible blood, one vomit, pain from the right loin into the groin. Any burning when you urinate?",
  "[SEG0009] person_3 (PATIENT): No, doctor. There is no burning.",
  "[SEG0010] person_2 (DOCTOR): Any fever, or chills?",
  "[SEG0011] person_3 (PATIENT): No. I have not felt feverish, and no chills.",
  "[SEG0012] person_2 (DOCTOR): What about chest pain, or shortness of breath?",
  "[SEG0013] person_3 (PATIENT): No, neither. My chest is fine, and my breathing is fine.",
  "[SEG0014] person_2 (DOCTOR): You've given me a clear picture of the pain. How are you feeling in yourself besides that?",
  "[SEG0015] person_3 (PATIENT): If I may say so, I feel like a wet rag.",
  "[SEG0016] person_2 (DOCTOR): A seven to eight, worse when you move, and thoroughly worn out. Does rest settle the pain at all?",
  "[SEG0017] person_3 (PATIENT): No, doctor. Resting does not really settle it. I did wonder whether I've overdone it in the yard yesterday, but this is nothing like a muscle strain.",
  "[SEG0018] person_4 (CAREGIVER): On the drive he told me his feet feel dead. Both of them.",
  "[SEG0019] person_3 (PATIENT): Yes. My feet feel dead, the two of them, since the ride. It may only be from sitting so long. Also, there is a frog in my throat since I retched.",
  "[SEG0020] person_2 (DOCTOR): I'll note the numb feet and the hoarse voice after the vomiting. We can come back to those. Do you have ongoing problems, any operations?",
  "[SEG0021] person_3 (PATIENT): I have high blood pressure, which is ongoing. I take lysinopril, twenty milligrams, by mouth, every morning. I have had no operations.",
  "[SEG0022] person_2 (DOCTOR): Lisinopril, twenty milligrams, once each morning by mouth, for the blood pressure, which we'll keep as an ongoing problem. Do you take it as prescribed?",
  "[SEG0023] person_3 (PATIENT): Yes, doctor. Every morning, without fail.",
  "[SEG0024] person_2 (DOCTOR): Any allergies to medicines, or to anything else?",
  "[SEG0025] person_3 (PATIENT): No. I have no known allergies.",
  "[SEG0026] person_4 (CAREGIVER): Getting here was a production, I'll tell you. The rain on the interstate had everyone crawling.",
  "[SEG0027] person_3 (PATIENT): Indeed. Between the trucks and the radio I could not hear myself think.",
  "[SEG0028] person_2 (DOCTOR): Mm. It has been a wet week.",
  "[SEG0029] person_4 (CAREGIVER): I was hoping to catch my granddaughter's soccer game after this. She's six, and they put her in goal, of all things.",
  "[SEG0030] person_3 (PATIENT): She is very determined. They play straight through the drizzle, which I rather admire.",
  "[SEG0031] person_1 (NURSE): Right. My nephew's team is the same, mud from head to toe.",
  "[SEG0032] person_4 (CAREGIVER): And the parking lot was packed. We circled twice before a spot opened.",
  "[SEG0033] person_2 (DOCTOR): Of. Well. Err, let me bring us back to the exam, sir.",
  "[SEG0034] person_2 (DOCTOR): Your abdomen is soft. There is tenderness over the right loin. I do not feel any guarding.",
  "[SEG0035] person_2 (DOCTOR): My working impression is renal colic, most likely a stone, though I cannot confirm that yet. Here is the plan I had in mind. An ultrasound of the kidney later this week, and ibuprofen, six hundred milligrams by mouth, as needed at home.",
  "[SEG0036] person_1 (NURSE): Doctor, sorry to cut in. The urine dip just came up. Large blood, trace protein, leukocytes negative, nitrites negative.",
  "[SEG0037] person_2 (DOCTOR): Thank you. That does change my plan. With large blood on the dip and the pain sitting at seven to eight, I don't want to wait for an ultrasound, and I won't send ibuprofen home. We'll do a CT of the abdomen and pelvis without contrast today, to look for a stone, and I'll give you one dose of oxycodone, five milligrams by mouth, here, for the pain.",
  "[SEG0038] person_3 (PATIENT): I understand, doctor. A scan today, and a pain tablet here. Thank you.",
  "[SEG0039] person_4 (CAREGIVER): I'll make sure he gets home after. He won't be driving.",
  "[SEG0040] person_2 (DOCTOR): Please drink plenty of water today. If the pain becomes unbearable, or if you vomit again and cannot keep fluids down, come back sooner rather than waiting.",
  "[SEG0041] person_2 (DOCTOR): I also want to see you back here in two days, whatever the scan shows. The front desk will book that.",
  "[SEG0042] person_3 (PATIENT): In two days. Yes. Is there anything else I should do in the meantime?",
  "[SEG0043] person_2 (DOCTOR): Just the fluids, the one dose of oxycodone now, the CT today, and that visit in two days. We'll go over the pictures then. My impression remains provisional renal colic until the scan is back.",
  "[SEG0044] person_1 (NURSE): I can give the oxycodone after you finish, and I'll book the CT for today and the return visit.",
  "[SEG0045] person_2 (DOCTOR): Yes, please do that. CT today, oxycodone five milligrams once by mouth, and follow-up in two days.",
  "[SEG0046] person_3 (PATIENT): You have been very clear, doctor. I appreciate the care.",
  "[SEG0047] person_4 (CAREGIVER): We'll be in the waiting room. Thank you, all of you."
 ],
